# What differs between one LoRA subject and the next. Everything else lives in
# studio/lora/_toolkit and is shared.
SUBJECT=ragnhild
MODEL=ragnhild
TRIGGER=ragnhild

# What anchors age and appearance when the trigger alone is not enough. The
# trigger carries the face; without this the model reaches for its own average
# of the word, which skews young. Read by _toolkit/shoots.rb.
#
# Specific, because with a weak adapter this carries most of the likeness. "Adult
# Norwegian woman in her 40s" is a phrase SDXL already has an average for, and a
# lightly-trained LoRA cannot overrule an average — it produced twelve pictures
# of a generic middle-aged woman.
#
# Structure rather than praise. "Beautiful" pulls CLIP toward the symmetrical
# stock-model face it saw most often, which fights the likeness instead of
# helping it; bone structure and colouring are things the model can actually
# place.
#
# No age. The FLUX LoRA trained on Replicate (anon987654321/ragnhild-flux)
# carries her age from the photographs, and "47 year old" on top of it doubles
# the ageing: at lora_scale 1.0 on fixed seeds the phrase turned hard light
# gaunt and haggard, and removing it kept the fringe and the face. Lowering the
# scale to 0.8 instead lost the fringe, so the phrase is the lever, not the
# adapter's strength.
DESCRIPTOR="Norwegian woman, slender, fine-boned, fair Nordic blonde, west coast Norway"
